%description:

RFC 9293 section 3.10.7.4 -- a zero-window probe is not acceptable and gets its ACK at once, even with
delayed ACKs on.

The rule: a segment with data that arrives while the receive window is zero is not acceptable, and
"an empty acknowledgment segment containing the current send sequence number and an
acknowledgment indicating the next sequence number expected to be received" is sent in reply. This
is how the sender of the probe learns the window. The ACK of a segment of 1 byte in an open window
is delayed (Rfc9293OneByteSegmentDelayedAck.test); this test guards the ACK of the probe, which
must stay at once.

Host A sends 5000 bytes with an MSS of 1000 bytes. The TS option takes 12 bytes of each segment, so
a full segment holds 988 bytes. Host B advertises a window of 3952 bytes, which is four full
segments, has delayed ACKs on, and reads nothing, so after four segments its window is zero and
host A holds the rest. Host A sends a probe of 1 byte when its persist timer expires.

Observation: host B sends the ACK of the probe in the next 0.05 s after the probe arrives, which is
before the delay timer of 200 ms can expire.

Expected result: PASS.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "PacketField.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

// At the TCP of a host a segment starts with its TCP header, so the data is what follows it.
static bool oneByteSegment(const MatchContext& context)
{
    const Packet *packet = context.event.packet;
    if (packet == nullptr)
        return false;
    return packet->getByteLength() - (long)evalPacketField(packet, "tcp.headerLength").doubleValueInUnit("B") == 1;
}

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("Rfc9293ZeroWindowProbeAckAtOnce")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.window == 0")
                  .first()
                  .describe("host B announces a zero window")
                  .within(1.0))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterEvent(oneByteSegment)
                  .first()
                  .describe("the zero-window probe of 1 byte arrives at host B")
                  .within(10.0))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.synBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .describe("the ACK of the probe, at once and not after the delay timer")
                  .within(0.05));
}

%activity:
EV << "Rfc9293ZeroWindowProbeAckAtOnce compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
**.tcp.mss = 1000
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 3952
*.host2.tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = true
*.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout = 200ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5000B
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST Rfc9293ZeroWindowProbeAckAtOnce: PASS
